Free options on GitHub:

1. openrouter-image-mcp (via DavidEasden/opencode-vision or devadathanmb's plugin)
Routes through OpenRouter using nvidia/nemotron-nano-12b-v2-vl:free — a free vision model on OpenRouter that requires no credits. This is probably your best bet — free API key, free model, no OpenCode Go credits burned.
GitHub
json

{
  "mcp": {
    "openrouter_image": {
      "type": "local",
      "command": ["npx", "openrouter-image-mcp"],
      "environment": {
        "OPENROUTER_API_KEY": "your-key",
        "OPENROUTER_MODEL": "nvidia/nemotron-nano-12b-v2-vl:free"
      }
    }
  }
}

2. NickRivers1983/opencode-vision (pip package)
MCP server that acts as a guide dog for text-only models, handling image analysis via PaddleOCR (SOTA deep learning, 100+ languages, ~15MB footprint) with Google Gemini 2.5 Flash Vision fallback. Gemini 2.5 Flash gives 1,500 free requests/day via Google AI Studio API key, no credit card required, and no OpenCode Go credits are consumed since the API call happens in the vision server, not through OpenCode's model proxy.
PyPI + 2
bash

pip install opencode-vision[paddle]